# src/

Koa Event-Driven application source.

## Directory layout

```
src/
├── main.ts               ← bootstrap: connect DB, start server
├── app.ts                ← builds the Koa app (importable from tests)
├── config/               ← env.ts + swagger.ts
├── errors/               ← AppError, NotFoundError, ValidationError, ConflictError
├── middlewares/           ← error-handler, validate-body (Zod/class-validator)
├── shared/               ← database clients, cache, auth, health
└── features/<module>/
    ├── <module>.routes.ts          ← manual DI wiring (the only file that creates instances)
    ├── commands/                   ← write-side command + handler
    ├── events/                     ← domain event classes
    ├── aggregates/                 ← aggregate root (state from events)
    ├── projections/                ← materialized read models
    ├── event-store/                ← append-only event log
    ├── dto/                        ← request validation
    └── infrastructure/             ← controller + outbox
```

## Putting files in features/

Each module in `features/` uses event sourcing:
- **`routes.ts`** creates every object and links them together (manual DI)
- **Controller** receives Koa contexts, builds commands, delegates to handler
- **Handler** orchestrates: creates aggregate, appends to event store, updates projection, enqueues outbox
- **Aggregate** is pure domain — creates events, applies them, tracks uncommitted changes
- **Projection** subscribes to events and maintains read-optimized views

Keep new modules inside `src/features/<module>/`.
